      "writtenOn": "2026-04-02T22:26:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe instead of doing these changes (i.e. introducing `for_each_initialized_cpu` and adjusting existing code to use it) in the same patch as the main thing done by this patch (i.e. waiting for host vCPUs to be kicked out), it would be better to do that in a separate patch, similarly to the patch aosp/4018594 which introduces `for_each_pkvm_guest_vcpu`?\n\nThen, this patch would become very small (just 2 lines of changes below), like aosp/4018595 already is, so we could combine this patch and aosp/4018595 into one patch? In fact, we could also squash them both into aosp/4018592, i.e. introduce `pkvm_wait_vcpu_kicked_out()` and use it in the same patch (that patch would be still simple and easy to review)?",
      "revId": "39840fc852a6c638680e44e91c12e588a949d6a6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "955b8a20_cb53e9f2",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/ept.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 201,
      "author": {
        "id": 4085392
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-03T02:44:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can do this in a separate patch. I think either this one or aosp/4018595 can be combined with aosp/4018592. Probably this one is better. But as this one and aosp/4018595 are having different Fixes tags, can we combine them with having two Fixes tags?",
      "parentUuid": "2e29285e_093b8a73",
      "revId": "39840fc852a6c638680e44e91c12e588a949d6a6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e9fc2bc_d1fba8f0",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/ept.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 201,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-03T11:44:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s ok to have two Fixes tags in one patch... OTOH, now thinking that if in future rebases we\u0027re gonna squash or reorder these patches into the original patches implementing host and guest TLB flushes, it might indeed be better to address host vCPUs in a separate patch(es) than guest vCPUs.\n\nSo e.g. yes, we can squash this patch into aosp/4018592, while keep aosp/4018595 a separate patch. (Or we can keep this patch also separate from aosp/4018592, I\u0027m fine with that too.)",
      "parentUuid": "955b8a20_cb53e9f2",
      "revId": "39840fc852a6c638680e44e91c12e588a949d6a6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
