      "lineNbr": 202,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-03T11:44:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`for_each_pkvm_host_vcpu_on_initialized_cpu` would be too mouthful, I think. :) And `for_each_pkvm_host_vcpu` wouldn\u0027t reflect that it is for initialized CPUs only...\n\nMaybe e.g. just `for_each_pkvm_initialized_cpu`? There is a 1:1 correspondence between physical CPUs and pKVM\u0027s host vCPUs, so it seems `for_each_pkvm_initialized_cpu` would sound rather clear, and it would rather make sense for it to provide host vCPU struct pointer along with just physical CPU number?",
